# Build artifacts
target/
**/node_modules/
# Patterns, not per-app paths, so the next example is covered: a local database carries NAV
# invoice numbers and must never ride into an image.
**/dist/
/data/
**/data/
**/*.db
**/*.db-*

# Secrets — the image gets its configuration from the environment.
# Both lines: an unanchored `.env` matches only the context root under Docker's rules, so the
# per-application ones need the `**/` — naming each one instead let the next example reintroduce it.
.env
**/.env

.git/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.sw?
